1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,511
Most shopping helps you buy what exists. Project Tesselle helps you get what you actually need.

2
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:15,381
It's a personal commerce agent built on Gemini, Google's Agent Development Kit, and Google Cloud.

3
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:25,561
1 · Inspiration - I start with a photo of my desk and a few words: the shelf leaves eighteen centimetres, I rent, so no drilling, about three thousand rupees.

4
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:35,501
2 · Intent - Gemini drafts a brief. MissionLock separates what must stay the same from what is flexible, and I confirm it.

5
00:00:38,783 --> 00:00:48,954
3 · Concept - The studio renders a concept, clearly labelled as an illustration. I pin an area and refine it, and the brief never changes silently.

6
00:00:53,350 --> 00:01:06,081
4 · Existing stock - An ADK graph workflow checks every route in parallel, with vector search over Gemini embeddings. This gorgeous bamboo station is rejected: twenty-two centimetres deep.

7
00:01:06,816 --> 00:01:14,907
5 · Maker request - So I ask a maker. I see exactly what they will receive. No name, no address, no photos of my home.

8
00:01:19,883 --> 00:01:25,974
6 · Counteroffer - The maker proposes its standard twenty-centimetre jig. MissionLock blocks it.

9
00:01:26,716 --> 00:01:35,807
7 · Resolution - I keep eighteen. The maker returns a revised layout that fits. The small price rise is a flexible decision, and it is mine.

10
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:42,361
8 · Device handoff - I can continue on my phone. The same decision follows me, with a spoken recap.

11
00:01:49,616 --> 00:01:59,427
9 · Approval - Approval is precise: one specification, one quote, one brief version. It is a sandbox order, so nothing is bought.

12
00:02:00,149 --> 00:02:04,920
Milestones and sample evidence stay tied to the approved brief.

13
00:02:09,182 --> 00:02:17,513
10 · Aftercare - After delivery, Gemini vision checks the photo against the checks I approved, and tells me what a photo cannot prove.

14
00:02:21,416 --> 00:02:26,707
Every agent step is on the record, with model, latency and tokens.

15
00:02:27,449 --> 00:02:35,860
Glasses capture - And capture can start anywhere, even from smart glasses. Snap it, ask, and Tesselle answers out loud.

16
00:02:39,082 --> 00:02:44,573
Project Tesselle. Imagine it. Keep what matters. Get it made.

